  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "For the function $f(x)$ defined by $f(x)=4x-6,$ find ${f}^{-1}(x).$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=4x-6\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=4y-6\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4y-6 \\\\ x+6 & =4y \\\\ \\frac{x+6}{4} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+6}{4}\n$$",
